One source-level blocker is emerging: the Unity request-70 server bounds connection count and request-byte wait, but performs the full response with synchronous `NetworkStream.Write` on the Unity coroutine/main thread and has no send timeout. A loopback peer that sends byte `70` and stops reading can therefore hang the player despite the pending-client cap; I’m validating the rest of the non-Unity surface before fixing the verdict.
